{
 "translation": "Shaukat is proud of his wealth, vain about his looks, and arrogant about his education. All this will be left behind. At three o'clock, Rahat and I reached Kishwar's place. Oh, seeing Kishwar, my heart was crushed. She was looking at me with strange, flustered, and lost eyes. She couldn't look me in the eye. Perhaps she was trying in vain to hide those tears that, having turned into blood, were shining on her cheeks. Although her eyes were dry, she was wearing a saffron-colored sari and pinning up her bun in front of the mirror. Seeing her in this flashy attire, I was scared that preparations for Sati were underway. But now I had arrived. I lovingly touched her chin, and she drowned in a dead-like laugh.",
